win10xbox: gdi32 exports every D3DKMT* thunk the native dxgi/d3d11/dxcore resolve by name

The native dxgi/d3d11 (machine-emu-d3d, Wine's gdi32 + win32u over core/user) fetch the D3DKMT* entry points of the real
gdi32.dll with GetProcAddress at run time; Wine's gdi32 exports only the subset it uses itself, so the first missing one
(D3DKMTGetSharedResourceAdapterLuid) made CreateDXGIFactory1 fail with STATUS_PROCEDURE_NOT_FOUND. On Windows each export
is a thin wrapper of the win32u syscall NtGdiDdDDI<same suffix> (one pointer argument), so every NtGdiDdDDI* of
win32u.spec without a D3DKMT counterpart gets a spec forward `D3DKMTxxx(ptr) win32u.NtGdiDdDDIxxx`. win32u's stubs are
syscall thunks the dispatcher passes through to the host's win32u by name (UseHostD3dkmt).

